        "title": "The baker who never sleeps",
        "body": "Rosa opens the padaria at four in the morning, long before the street wakes up. By six the first loaves are cooling on the counter, and the neighbors start knocking on the window.",
        "sectionNumber": 1,
        "sectionCount": 2,
        "level": "a2",
        "readingProgress": 0.5,
        "translation": "Rosa abre a padaria às quatro da manhã, muito antes de a rua acordar. Às seis, os primeiros pães esfriam no balcão e os vizinhos começam a bater na janela."
      },
      {
        "title": "The baker who never sleeps",
        "body": "Rosa says the dough decides when the bread is ready. All she does is wait, and she has had thirty years of practice.",
